WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:07.680
Speaker 1: Let's start with the most fun possible
segment we ever do, which is a review of where

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.890
we are with the coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.040
I know it's really a party.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.240
We haven't done a review of covid cases and
deaths lately because it's just been so busy

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.240
on the show.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.550
But now, in the context of some declining
vaccination and changing mass guidelines,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.859
which we will get to, this is worth doing.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:32.400
I believe we are now three weeks from a massive
reduction in covid cases and just a little

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.140
more than three weeks from a massive reduction
in covid deaths.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.600
Now, keep me honest on this.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.850
This means May 19, three weeks from today,
I've marked it in the calendar.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.010
I believe covid numbers will be looking really
good in the United States.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.890
And we're going to come back and see if that
actually happens.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.550
Let's start with cases and then we'll talk
about what's going on.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:56.310
So to begin with, as a reminder, the U.S.
has had essentially four case spikes.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:01:02.720
The first was that first spike in March of
twenty twenty, the second in July of 2012,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.000
summer of twenty twenty, the third and the
biggest in the winter of 2020 into January

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.050
of twenty twenty one.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:13.730
And that is case has started to come down
rapidly during the vaccination phase in February

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.750
and in March, cases kicked back up a little
bit.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.760
Why did this happen?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.880
Well, it's believed that it was because some
people started going nuts too soon even though

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.540
they weren't vaccinated.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.830
And then also we had that British variant,
the B one one seven variant in the northeast

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.580
of the U.S., in Michigan and a few other places.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.770
And it was actually starting to outrun vaccines.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.400
We seem to have turned that around.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.729
Case numbers now coming down in Michigan.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:47.549
It now seems we vaccinated quickly enough
that we are back into some semblance of control

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:50.190
in what is big picture and out of control
situation.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:54.720
Remember that the vaccines work well against
all the variants, to some degree less so against

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.570
the South African variant, but still does
does.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:02.970
Well, cases are now down about 20 percent
from that mini peak a month ago.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.049
So from that little peak, we're already down
20 percent.

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:12.959
We're down 78 percent in cases per day from
the big peak in the middle of January.

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:14.700
That should continue down.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:21.140
Now, the death curve, the death curve has
been more nuanced, but it also didn't really

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.300
experience any resurgence in the past couple
of months.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.110
Even though cases went back up, deaths did
not.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:32.450
Deaths peaked in late January, around 3400
per day.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.510
Just an incredible, horrifying number.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.020
They are now down to about seven hundred and
twenty five deaths a day.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.390
Still terrible, but continuing to decline.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.599
We are down about 80 percent in daily deaths,
but 20 percent of that peak is still a lot.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:52.620
The death decline can take longer because,
I mean, quite morbidly, it takes time to die

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.290
from covid.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.440
So there are people who have been sick for
a while who will continue to die even as more

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.490
people are protected by the vaccine.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:05.290
People who would have died in June, did they
not get vaccinated today?

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.640
It takes a little time to see the impact of
that.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:12.580
But by Memorial Day, hopefully death numbers
will also be really low.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:19.510
Now, unfortunately, these case and death declines
are coming as we are seeing reduced vaccination

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.510
numbers.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.150
This is not because of the brief pause to
the Johnson and Johnson vaccine.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.740
It is not because there aren't vaccines available.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:33.700
This is increasingly a demand issue after
a long period of vaccination increasing all

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:38.170
the way up to an average of three and a half
million doses per day, we were hoping we would

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.900
get to four or even five million doses per
day.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.240
We did not.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:48.080
We are now back down to two point seven million
doses per day, continuing to decline only

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.810
two point one and one point seven million
doses per day in each of the last two days.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.390
There are lots of vaccination centers in blue
states, red states, north, south, everywhere,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.800
saying you don't need an appointment, just
show up and get a vaccine.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.510
We should soon see approval of the Phizer
vaccine for people aged 12 to 15, hopefully

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.700
Moderna as well.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.610
That will add people to the demand.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:17.630
But we are getting to where more and more
of the people that want a vaccine have gotten

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.049
it, or at least the first dose waiting on
a second.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:23.730
So we are now going to need new initiatives
to encourage people to go out and get the

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.730
vaccine.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:29.080
Today, I will be talking about Joe Rogan's
recent anti vaccine comments, which I find

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.240
very dangerous.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:35.100
Many of you wrote to me about them saying,
David, why won't you criticize your friend

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.100
Joe Rogan?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.100
All right.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.100
Well, we're going to do it today.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.420
It's very dangerous.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.800
We do not need things said now that will encourage
people not to get vaccinated.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.800
So that will.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.040
Yes, I will talk about my friend Joe Rogan.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.890
We will talk about it today.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:53.979
But even if we can keep doing two million
doses a day, we're still going to be looking

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:56.260
quite good by the middle of June.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.830
And that's where we are today.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.920
This stuff matters.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.970
We now have.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:06.830
As I told you earlier, more relaxed or rather,
as I told you yesterday, we would get and

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.330
we will discuss in detail later today, I realize
it's unclear to say I told you earlier.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.330
I told you yesterday.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.870
And now we have the new guidelines.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.970
We have more relaxed mass guidelines because
people have been getting vaccinated because

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.910
the vaccines are so effective.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.380
At the same time, we're nowhere near out of
the global catastrophe.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:29.620
I'm putting up on the screen the chart, the
case chart from India, which we discussed

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.620
on a previous show.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.430
And it is a disaster.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.270
People are literally dying in the streets.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:44.710
In India, a video came out of two sons on
a motorcycle transporting their dead mother,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.940
holding her upright on the motorcycle because
all services she died of covid.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.419
All services are collapsing in India.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:55.570
Even in Canada, cases have been spiking and
things have not been looking so good.

00:05:55.570 --> 00:06:02.280
So this will be a continued and long global
process, which will hopefully look much better

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.830
in some countries.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.639
As soon as a few weeks from now, we're going
to get to the masking.

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:09.880
We're going to get the vaccination later.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:47.210
But that's where we are on cases 

00:06:47.210 --> 00:07:57.340
and deaths.

